A||||6||RacinRob||Dim pass. side headlight||||1||
Z||000000||RacinRob||08-08-2001||11:57 AM||||I'm having a problem were the passenger side headlight is really dim.... I just changed them and it didn't help.  I really have no idea what this could be.<P>thanks for any help<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TylerB11||08-08-2001||12:23 PM||||possibly a bad headlight relay or fuse..if not, check your wiring(bad ground?)||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-08-2001||12:27 PM||||usually a dim lite is a bad ground, clean area and put in new screw. also not a bad idea to put a dab of undercoating over it after.||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||08-08-2001||12:31 PM||||Sounds like the ground (black) wire going to that socket isn't connected to a good ground. So the juice is taking a return path through the other filament in the bulb.<P>Inspect the socket for good connections to the mating terminals on the headlight, and from there to ground.  <P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||RacinRob||08-08-2001||12:32 PM||||where do they ground?<P><BR>there is also a lot of black crap in the sockets... I've been tring to clean some of that out. is there any way to get the pins out of the plastic socket?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by RacinRob (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||08-08-2001||12:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by StuGood:<BR><B>Inspect the socket for good connections to the mating terminals on the headlight...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>This has caused me problems, before. The three terminals can corrode and make a poor connection. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||08-08-2001||01:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RacinRob:<BR><B>where do they ground?<P><BR>there is also a lot of black crap in the sockets... I've been tring to clean some of that out. is there any way to get the pins out of the plastic socket?<P><BR>[This message has been edited by RacinRob (edited 08-08-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>There is a grounding screw on the outside vertical surface of the headlight bucket. Clean the surrounding area and wires and screw. you may want to coat them with dielectric compound and reattach.<P>The 'black crap' is the factory dielect compound, electric parts cleaner will clean it but if you don't do much electrical work it is cost prohivitive. Go and buy a new plug and install it using new dielectric compound.<BR>||||reg||1
